Looking at each case, I need to set up the CCD Annex I present-value equation, then solve by bisection.

**Working through each case:**

**Case 1:** Fee at t=0 on repayment side → 9900 = 450·AF(24,r). Bisection narrows from 5%→10%→8.5%→8.84%.

**Case 2:** Overdraft: €30 interest + €25 fee = €55/mo, bullet principal at month 3. High fixed fees over short duration drive APRC well above the nominal rate.

**Case 3:** PMT = 1500×0.015/(1−1.015⁻¹²) = €137.52. No extra fees → APRC = effective annual rate of 18% nominal monthly.

**Case 4:** Financed fee adds €200 to principal → repayment = 5200×1.08 = 5616 at t=1yr. Single discount trivially solvable.

